      "url": "https://www.cpf.gov.sg/service/article/how-much-is-my-basic-retirement-sum",
      "retrieved": "2026-08-20",
      "note": "CPF Board publishes the BRS for every cohort and states 'your Full Retirement Sum is double your BRS'. Only the BRS column below is transcribed; FRS and ERS are derived in cpfdata.py from CPF's own rules, so a slip in one derived figure is not expressible. Cross-checked against CPF Board's Retirement Sums PDF (2017-2022) and the current retirement-sum page (2025-2027)."
    },
    "frs_minimum_sum_series": {
      "title": "CPFB | Full Retirement Sum by 55th birthday, 1 July 1995 to 1 January 2027",
      "url": "https://www.cpf.gov.sg/service/sfc/servlet.shepherd/version/download/068IW000002bHNJYA2",
      "retrieved": "2026-08-20",
      "note": "CPF Board's own document. It lists the pre-2016 Minimum Sum and the post-2016 Full Retirement Sum in ONE continuous column headed 'Full Retirement Sum' — which is the primary evidence that they are the same series under two names. It also shows the revision date moving from 1 July to 1 January: the 1 July 2015 cohort is followed directly by 1 January 2017. Transcribed independently of retirement_sums_brs_history, so the eleven overlapping years are a cross-check."
    },
    "medisave_changes_2016": {
      "title": "MOH / CPF | Changes to the Medisave Scheme (factsheet, CPF Advisory Panel recommendations)",
      "url": "https://www.cpf.gov.sg/content/dam/web/member/infohub/documents/FactsheetonChangestotheMedisaveScheme.pdf",
      "retrieved": "2026-08-20",
      "note": "The primary source for the OTHER 'minimum sum'. Two different things happened on 1 January 2016 and they are routinely conflated: the Medisave Minimum Sum was REMOVED outright ('we will remove the Medisave Minimum Sum (MMS) from 1 January 2016'), while it was the Medisave Contribution CEILING that was renamed the Basic Healthcare Sum ('the Medisave Contribution Ceiling (MCC) will be renamed as the Basic Healthcare Sum (BHS)'). Saying the MMS became the BHS is wrong."
    },
    "ers_rule": {
      "title": "CPFB | What is the Enhanced Retirement Sum (ERS)?",
      "url": "https://www.cpf.gov.sg/service/article/what-is-the-enhanced-retirement-sum-ers",
      "retrieved": "2026-08-20",
      "note": "Quote: 'The ERS amount is not dependent on your age or the year you turn 55 years old. It increases yearly on 1 January.' and 'the ERS amount is double the current year's Full Retirement Sum (FRS)'. The ERS is therefore NOT a cohort attribute the way BRS and FRS are \u2014 it is the top-up ceiling in force that calendar year for every member aged 55 and above. It was 3x the BRS through 2024 and became 4x (= 2x FRS) on 1 January 2025."
    }
  },

